  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/tra200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Tra 202.15 Disqualification of a Representative",
  "priorExpiration": "1999-01-28",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Tra 202.15 Disqualification of a Representative.\n\n(a) An individual shall be prohibited from acting as a representative before the department in the pending proceeding if, after notice and an opportunity for hearing, the presiding officer finds that the individual has engaged in misconduct concerning the hearing.\n\n(b) A finding of misconduct shall be based on acts or failures to act which result in one or more of the following consequences in a pending proceeding:\n\n(1) Disruption of the orderly conduct of procedure; or\n\n(2) Prejudice to the substantive rights of other parties.\n\nSource. #4174, eff 12-1-86; EXPIRED 12-1-90\n\nNew. #5563, eff 1-28-93, EXPIRED: 1-28-99\n\nNew. #7927-A, eff 7-26-03",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/tra200.html"
